250901:

Neutron "trajectories" has been implemented. This includes the use of
DEBUG_SCATTER and DEBUG_STATE. These are only called during componen traces.

However, a DEBUG_STATE call is interjected in our custom trace code, after the
trace of each component, since not every component will call SCATTER for 
debug purposes. (For example, our SourceMaxwell.)

The trajectory tracing is actually using some global values for the capture,
to provide som custom context for "_ext_hook" functions.

McPlot: 

Having fetched both display and trace output, which are both represented as
line segments, we also need to fetch the plot data.

Plot data is output in the Comp_Save sections, and uses the following API:

MCDETECTOR mcdetector_out_0D
MCDETECTOR mcdetector_out_1D
MCDETECTOR mcdetector_out_2D

We should try and map out what the parameters are, and simply re-implement
these three functions. As we basically just need to output to our own
screen logger, somehow. (Essentially a simplified version of the mcplot
outputs.)

The MCDETECTOR is a big catch-all struct called "mcdetector_struct".

mcdetector_out_0D(char *t, double p0, double p1, double p2, char *c, Coords pos, Rotation rot, int index):

t: title
p0: count data ptr
p1: probability data ptr
p2: probability squared data ptr
c/pos/rot/index: compname, transform & index of the monitor component [what is this used for? Expect monitor output in local coordinates]


mcdetector_out_1D(char *t, char *xl, char *yl, char *xvar, double x1, double x2, long n, double *p0, double *p1, double *p2, char *f,
    char *c, Coords pos, Rotation rot, int index):

t: title
xl: x axis label
yl: y axis label
xvar: name of variable
x1: xmin
x2: xmax
n: bin count
p0: (see above) ptr into 1d array, e.g. [i] between 0, n
p1: (see above)
p2: (see above)
f: filename
c/pos/rot/index: see above

mcdetector_out_2D(char *t, char *xl, char *yl, double x1, double x2, double y1, double y2, long m, long n, double *p0, double *p1, double *p2, char *f,
    char *c, Coords pos, Rotation rot, int index)

t: title
xl: x axis label
yl: y axis label
x1: xmin
x2: xmax
y1: ymin
y2: ymax
m: bin count x-axis
n: bin count y-axis
p0: (see above) ptr into 2D array, e.g. used through [i][j] between [0,0] and [m,n]
p1: (see above)
p2: (see above)
f: filename
c/pos/rot/index: see above




250901:

Component "mcdisplay" calls have been impmenented. The "_ext_hook" functions 
calls some global values behind the scenes, in order to preserve the simcore.h 
APIs in their original state. This make the modified simcore.h more comparable
to what exists across various mcstas files.


250820:

Design principles:

- Keeping as much code out of the code-generated sections
- Being able to debug generated code easilly
- Keeping the dev cycle tight and fast (build -> run -> debug)


250816:

It is possible to call the "mcdisplay functions", and they do seem to work
correctly. The result is printing to the console, and we want to capture that
data into an array of line segment pairs. (Arguably, multiple arrays
depending on type, but for now.)

The current "component" API and corresponding library functions:
                                                NOTE:
    #define magnify     mcdis_magnify           does nothing
    #define line        mcdis_line              very useful, produces the segment (anchor) pair
    #define dashed_line mcdis_dashed_line       falls back to mcdis_line
    #define multiline   mcdis_multiline         pruduces a sequence of anchors (...)
    #define rectangle   mcdis_rectangle         falls back to mcdis_multiline
    #define box         mcdis_box               falls back to mcdis_rectangle and mcdis_multiline
    #define circle      mcdis_circle            outputs an abstract code to the terminal
    #define Circle      mcdis_Circle            falls back to mcdis_line
    #define cylinder    mcdis_cylinder          falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line
    #define cone        mcdis_cone              falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line
    #define sphere      mcdis_sphere            falls back to mcdis_Circle, mcdis_line

Typical signatures would be: 

    void mcdis_line(double x1, double y1, double z1, double x2, double y2, double z2);
    void mcdis_circle(char *plane, double x, double y, double z, double r);
    void mcdis_multiline(int count, ...);
    void mcdis_Circle(double x, double y, double z, double r, double nx, double ny, double nz);

Thus we need to replace the intrinsic ones to produce line-segment anchor pairs, specifically:

    mcdis_line
    mcdis_multiline

In addition, the use of mcdis_circle, and perhaps a few others (not used 
in PSI_DMC, apparantly), should be transitioned to mcdis_Circle (capital C).
The latter generates lines, while the former prints a "circle" call,
effectively delegating implementation to the external tool. But this API
is bad and also redundant.
We can re-implement these calls to forward to the more complete mcdis_ calls.


